  "asr_text": "You call me mad? I am perfectly sane. My illness sharpened my senses. It did not weaken my mind. I hear everything in heaven and earth. Listen, and judge how calmly I tell you what happened. The old man shared my house. I loved him. He had never hurt me, and I wanted none of his money. Only his eye troubled me. Pale blue, with a cloudy film, a vulture's eye. You understand? That eye had to go. For seven nights, at midnight, I opened his bedroom door so slowly that it made no sound. Then I let a thin ray from my lantern touch his face. Always the eye was closed. What could I do? I hated the eye, not the man. On the eighth night, I smiled at my own patience. Then my thumb slipped against the lantern fastening.",
